@HardwareCanucks You say that to compare FE to FE so you dont compare pre overclocked cards. But the 20 Series FEs are not running stock settings either!
And with GPU Boost, the cards with the same GPUs boost to about the same performance, IF the cooling is sufficient. Which it is for the 20 Series FE but is not for the 1080 TI FE. 
Youre digging for another moon, arent you?

 @damienk2372  it is a problem when one of the cards is chosen to be benchmarked with cooler that throttles ... in which case you dont benchmark the card but the cooler instead.
That comparison would fly if both cards used same cooler but as it is the 20series has to be compared to aib card with axial fan cooler that wont throttle its performance ...

